// GPDK045 native Cadence adaptation; NOT a performance-matched paper reproduction.
// Missing device sizes/values use recorded defaults; see plan.json and classification CSV.
// Explicit body nets, including deliberately floating bodies, are preserved.
// PDK_BULK_N/PDK_BULK_P, where present, require an external bulk bias.
// Evidence: /projects/2022B4AA1300P/SchematicGeneration/Papers_dataset/consolidated_paper_dataset_final_locked/agnibha_mixed_pdk_20261008/cases/p03_adaptive_ldo_complete
// Original comments below describe the pre-conversion topology:
// original: Manually traced from batch1/images/p03_adaptive_ldo_complete.png, 2026-10-01.
// original: Topology-only golden netlist; not a native Cadence export or simulation deck.
// original: MOS order D G S B; NPN order C B E. Current flows first pin to second.
// original: All 24 MOS symbols have body pins. Open bodies are separate named nets;
// original: they are not silently tied to source or a supply.
// original: User confirmed the floating reference-stage bodies and NM5/PM12 gate tie.
// original: User also confirmed the separate open bodies on PM7-PM12, M13, NM2-NM4,
// original: M17 and M18. They intentionally remain floating, exactly as drawn.
// original: Dashed red stage boxes and the drawing grid are not electrical wires.
// original: Reference and startup block.
// original: Error amplifier and adaptive tail-current bias.
// original: Adaptive branch. FB is the output divider, NOT NM5's gate.
// original: Pass transistor and output network.
// original: I31 is the image's instance label on a resistor symbol, r=600; not a source.
simulator lang=spectre
global 0
include "/linuxeda_new/c2scadence/FOUNDRY/analog/45nm/models/spectre/gpdk045.scs" section=tt

